        "runId": "ada-en-20261110-o0ph8fryncjmw9u91va",
        "model": "GPT-6"
      },
      "text": ", Sunday: Orinoco River Delta"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:2e780f63f4172747",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "9a75c93b309480cab515b04db2b84bdc7d36daadf859eb9e5ff93c9fa2043dbd",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261110-o0ph8fryncjmw9u91va",
        "model": "GPT-6"
      },
      "text": "After breakfast, transfer to the airport and fly to the Orinoco Delta. Then transfer to the Boca de Uracoa pier and travel by motorboat through the channels.\n\nThe Orinoco rises near Mount Delgado Chalbaud in the Parima region by the Brazilian border and empties into the Gulf of Paria in the Atlantic Ocean. In its lower reaches, the river splits into hundreds of channels, forming a delta of about 41,000 sq km. The river crosses the subequatorial zone, is fed mainly by rainfall and varies considerably in level throughout the year. In the dry season, smaller tributaries turn into chains of still pools.\n\nAlong the way, you may see floating islands, many birds, monkeys and, with luck, river bottlenose dolphins. Check in and have lunch on arrival. In the afternoon, take part in a short jungle survival session. Return for dinner.\n\nMeals: breakfast, lunch and dinner."
